<title>UK: BP in Portuguese retail joint venture.</title>
<headline>BP in Portuguese retail joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum said on Monday it had formed a 50:50 joint venture with Portuguese grocery retailer Modelo Continente SGPS, owned by Sonae to build stores alongside BP filling stations in Portugal.</p>
<p>The venture will start with a number of pilot sites, which, if successful, are to be followed by another 100 stores.</p>
<p>The stores will offer a wider products range than traditional convenience stores and would be able to satisfy a large part of families' shopping needs, BP said.</p>
<p>This is BP's second venture with a major European retailer. In September 1996, it signed an agreement with Britain's Safeway for 100 jointly-owned food and fuel sites.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
